{
  "summary": "Introduces support for target-specific custom mutators in Bitcoin Core's libFuzzer harness and implements a structure-aware custom mutator for PSBTs. The mutator deserializes inputs into key-value maps across global, input, and output scopes, applies tailored mutations to valid field components, and reserializes them for the `partially_signed_transaction_deserialize` target.",
  "problem": "The existing PSBT fuzz target relies on purely raw byte-level mutations, which almost never produce well-formed key-value maps with valid keydata (such as public keys, xpubs, and signatures). As a result, inputs are rejected at the shallow parser stage and deeper PSBT deserialization logic is rarely reached.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author notes in PR description: 'Byte-level mutations rarely produce well-formed key-value maps with valid keydata (pubkeys, xpubs, control blocks, DER signatures, etc), so most inputs are rejected early and the deeper per-field parsing is rarely reached.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The custom mutator was ported from bitcoinfuzz with LLM assistance, and the harness changes conditionally configure `LLVMFuzzerCustomMutator` without impacting non-libFuzzer fuzzing engines.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds a structure-aware custom mutator for the PSBT fuzz target, ported from bitcoinfuzz, along with general support in the fuzz harness for target-specific libFuzzer mutators. Currently, raw byte-level mutations fail early on basic PSBT validation, preventing the fuzzer from exploring deep per-field parsing logic. The PR enables fuzz testing of complex PSBT key-value maps and field deserialization paths.",
